; qwen38-heed-grounded-run.fk — the whole lane, live: real Qwen weights write a
; knowledge query into their own stream, the cursor recognizes it, the grounded
; nodeid-rag-v2 index answers, and the model writes its reply from the
; non-borrowable answer reserve that the hit opened.
;
; This is the run the floor has been one adapter wide since morning. The
; difference from qwen38-heed-cursor-run.fk is exactly one function value:
; fhg-lookup instead of fcmg-heed-lookup-nothing.
;
; Two ledgers: query budget 48, answer reserve 32. A hit opens the reserve and
; cuts the unused query fuel; the answer is written from steps query verbosity
; could never have reached.
;
; No logit executes anything. q38-forward returns an argmax over a distribution;
; the cursor recognizes bytes; this carrier retrieves. model-executed reads 0.
;
; Telemetry is bounded and non-content: counts, statuses, and a SHA-256 of the
; reply — never the reply.
;
; Effectful: opens a sealed 29GB GGUF, drives the GPU, and reads the grounded
; index. Do not preflight.
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/form-cli-model-generate.fk form/form-stdlib/model-registry.bml

(fcmg-heed-witness-grounded
    (mr-path (mr-find "qwen38-q8"))
    "To look a fact up in the Form body, write exactly <|form:knowledge-query|>your question<|/form:knowledge-query|> and then stop. Look up whether Sema keeps memory of you between visits, then answer in one sentence."
    48
    32)
